Package: hd-plymouth
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Erik Van Hamme <erik.vanhamme@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: plymouth, plymouth-label, initramfs-tools, fontconfig, python3, hd-art, hd-fonts
Conflicts: desktop-base
Enhances: hd-desktop
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Description: HyprDebian boot splash
 The plymouth theme hyprdebian, which looks like the lock screen of hyprlock
 in hd-desktop: the Emerald wallpaper of hd-art, and for a password, such as
 the one of an encrypted ZFS dataset that the initramfs asks for, an input
 field with a translucent black fill, an orange outline and blue dots, in
 JetBrains Mono of hd-fonts.
 .
 The package makes hyprdebian the theme of plymouth: it diverts
 /etc/plymouth/plymouthd.conf of plymouth and writes its own, and has
 initramfs-tools rebuild the initramfs, with the theme and its fonts. It
 conflicts with desktop-base, whose themes it replaces.
